<title>MEXICO: Mexico hikes aid to grain producers by 3 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Mexico hikes aid to grain producers by 3 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican government boosted its 1997 aid to grain farmers to 3.5 billion pesos from an originally budgeted 500 million pesos, the National Farm Council (CNA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;There are two factors for the increased budget. It reflects the greater production of grains and the fall in prices in international markets,&quot; CNA Vice-President Luis Cardenas Fonseco told reporters at the CNA annual assembly.</p>
<p>He said Mexico's congress approved the additional financial support.</p>
<p>&quot;We've had to spend more than we expected. We've increased the area for planting, but now we need more funding because of the drop in international prices,&quot; Agriculture Secretary Francisco Labastida said at the assembly.</p>
<p>Mexico has boosted plantings to reduce its dependence on imports of basic grains.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
